    <h2><a href="articles/fractional-grid-graph-paper--generate-your-own-pdfs-">Fractional grid graph paper (generate your own PDFs)</a></h2>
    <div class="variables">
    <div class="date">@date=2026-10-09</div>
    <div class="tags">@tags=<a href="tags/graph-paper">graph-paper</a>, <a href="tags/pdf">pdf</a>, <a href="tags/python">python</a>, <a href="tags/print">print</a></div>
    </div>
    <article>
        <p><img data-src="images/20261009100133 dot grid.png" alt="20261009100133 dot grid.png" style="max-width: 100%;max-height:40vh;" /></p>
<p>So this is some nerdy dotted paper. Note that this image is a zoom in, the dots are smaller and lighter when printed. </p>
<p>One <strong>base unit</strong> (1 cm, 1 inch, or quarter inch). On top of that you get 4×, 1×, ½×, and ¼× gray dots, plus a red ⅓× overlay and green every-third 1× dot so you can actually see the 3 vs 4 rhythm. </p>
<p>You can print this in a4 or letter, and in any one of the 3 base units. </p>
<p>Of course, the code is open so you can tweak the dot sizes and colors to your heart&#39;s content. </p>
<p>Or, you can just dig into the output directory and download the page and run with it.</p>
<p>The pdfs have two duplicate pages in each to help make it easy to do double sided. </p>
<p>Repo: <a href="https://github.com/RobKohr/fractional-grid-graph-paper">fractional-grid-graph-paper</a></p>

    </article>
    
